# GitTrace environment template.
# Copy to .env only if you need to change something. Never commit .env.

# Model triage (gittrace scan) through LiteLLM; a local Ollama model by default.
# `--model` on the command line wins over GITTRACE_MODEL. `--no-llm` skips the model.
GITTRACE_MODEL=ollama/llama3.1:8b
# Summaries (gittrace explain) use their own model; GITTRACE_MODEL does not apply to them.
GITTRACE_EXPLAIN_MODEL=ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b
# Seconds to wait for one reply (default 120; the first call also loads the model).
# GITTRACE_LLM_TIMEOUT=120
# Where Ollama listens, if not http://localhost:11434 (read by LiteLLM).
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434

# Route the model calls above through the open-source Respan Gateway instead of
# LiteLLM directly: one endpoint for every vendor, with fallback routes. The
# gateway then uses the model names, provider keys (OPENAI_API_KEY,
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, ...) and routes of a gateway.toml. No
# Respan account or credits are involved. See README "Model layer through the
# Respan Gateway".
# GITTRACE_GATEWAY=1
# A gateway.toml to read; without it the gateway is built from the provider keys
# in the environment, plus local Ollama. A gateway.toml in the folder you run
# GitTrace from is never read.
# GITTRACE_GATEWAY_CONFIG=/path/to/gateway.toml
